DAY 24 – POLYMORPHISM

1. POLYMORPHISM

Polymorphism means the same operation can behave
differently depending on the object or data type.


2. DUCK TYPING

Duck Typing means Python focuses on whether an object
has the required method rather than checking its
exact type.


3. OPERATOR OVERLOADING

Operator Overloading means using operators such as
+ and * with different behaviors depending on
the objects involved.


4. METHOD OVERLOADING

Method Overloading means having different parameter
behaviors for the same method.

In Python, this can be simulated using:

• Default arguments
• Variable-length arguments


5. METHOD OVERRIDING

Method Overriding means redefining a parent class
method in a child class.

The child class provides its own implementation
of the method.


6. SPECIAL METHODS

Python provides special methods that can be used
for operator overloading and object representation.

Important special methods include:

__add__() → Used for addition behavior.

__mul__() → Used for multiplication behavior.

__str__() → Used to define the string representation
of an object.


KEY TAKEAWAY

Polymorphism allows the same operation to produce
different behaviors in Python.

Duck Typing → Focuses on required behavior.

Operator Overloading → Gives operators different
behaviors for different objects.

Method Overloading → Simulated using default or
variable-length arguments.

Method Overriding → Redefines a parent method
in a child class.